FINDINGS: #C656 collector-new-tools 7ab61f3. My two findings on e733d46 are fixed, with tests (probe: seeding runs 2, 10 and 44 all reach back 0.58 h, the last merged run plus the overlap; the steps page's where is the same across runs). Suite 1254/1254 green (capped). One new finding, from the move to recorded answers:
1. MEDIUM-HIGH, collector/delta.mjs ingestCalls (and mergeRun, which then writes state.at = mark.at): a delta query whose recorded answer has next !== null, with no later record continuing it, is taken as the whole delta. Probe (scratchpad c656-probe.mjs): one steps answer of 200 documents with next "abc123" and no page 2 -> ingestCalls {delta: 1}, one page saved, nothing marks it incomplete. The task asks the run to follow every nextCursor, but that is the model's discipline only: a run that errors or runs out of budget mid-chain gets merged, the next delta starts after the missed documents, and they are lost until the next sweep heals them (up to 3 days plus a sweep). Fix: per planned query, follow the recorded chain (cursor null -> next -> ... -> next null); if any chain is unfinished, return incomplete, and mergeRun neither lays nor advances state.at (as for an unsealed export), so the next run re-reads from the same since. Tests: an unfinished chain is not merged and state.at stays; a finished two-page chain is merged. Plus a mutation check.
